<title>SPAIN: Sevillana posts 23.5 pct rise in 1996 net profit.</title>
<headline>Sevillana posts 23.5 pct rise in 1996 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996 results for Spain's</p>
<p>Sevillana de Electricidad, in billions of pesetas, unless</p>
<p>stated:</p>
<p> Net taxed				 20.41    up   23.5 pct</p>
<p> Turnover				 290.14    up    2.6 pct</p>
<p> Operating profit			45.19    up   11.1 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: Results correspond to the parent company.</p>
<p>Sevillana said it would pay a total 1996 dividend of 50 pesetas gross versus 40 pesetas the year earlier.</p>
<p>The firm said results were staisfactory due to increased demand, good management and efficiency measures.</p>
<p>Debt was reduced by more than 185 billion pesetas, or 60 percent, in 1996.</p>
</text>
